(a) The following fees are established:

(1) with respect to a license for which the licensee failed to notify the director of the information required under AS 21.27.025 and within the time period required by AS 21.27.025, if notification is received

(A) one - 60 days late, $50;

(B) 61 - 120 days late, $100; or

(C) more than 120 days late, $200;

(2) issuance of a certification, $25;

(3) acceptance of service of process, $25;

(4) three-year rating bureau license, $6,000;

(5) delayed renewal penalty fee to reinstate a license that lapsed, and that has not been suspended or revoked, if payment is overdue by

(A) one - 60 days, $100; or

(B) over 60 days, $200;

(6) with respect to an application to reinstate a revoked license, if received within six months after the revocation, the application fee plus a reinstatement fee of $500;

(7) filing of a certified annual financial statement by an alien surplus lines insurer not on the list described in AS 21.34.040(c)(7), $100;

